# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository.
#
# This is a real CI lesson, not housekeeping. You are on Windows, where git
# checks files out with CRLF endings. GitHub's runners are Linux, where a
# stray \r breaks shell scripts in a way that produces genuinely baffling
# errors ("$'\r': command not found"). Storing LF in the repo means the
# runner always sees LF, whatever your editor does locally.
#
# See COURSE/TROUBLESHOOTING.md, "Windows jobs fail, Linux passes".
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must never be mangled.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
